#### 规则概述
此规则用于检测未被正确使用或可能导致内存泄漏的结构体。在创建结构体实例后，如果未能恰当地释放或使用，可能导致资源的耗尽。

##### 规则意义
确保结构体实例被正确处理，可以避免潜在的内存泄露和性能问题，维护代码的可读性和可维护性。

##### 错误示例
'''go
package main

type MyStruct struct {
    Field1 string
}

func main() {
    s := MyStruct{Field1: "Hello"}
    // 忘记使用或处理s
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''go
package main

import "fmt"

type MyStruct struct {
    Field1 string
}

func main() {
    s := MyStruct{Field1: "Hello"}
    fmt.Println(s.Field1) // 正确使用结构体
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to detect structures that are not being used properly or may lead to memory leaks. If a structure instance is created but not properly released or used, it may result in resource exhaustion.

##### Rule Meaning
Ensuring that structure instances are handled correctly can prevent potential memory leaks and performance issues, as well as maintain the readability and maintainability of the code.

##### Error Example
'''go
package main

type MyStruct struct {
    Field1 string
}

func main() {
    s := MyStruct{Field1: "Hello"}
    // Forgot to use or handle s
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''go
package main

import "fmt"

type MyStruct struct {
    Field1 string
}

func main() {
    s := MyStruct{Field1: "Hello"}
    fmt.Println(s.Field1) // Correct usage of the structure
}
'''

