#### 规则概述
该规则旨在确保Go模块的依赖关系不会在未授权的情况下被更改，从而保护项目的代码完整性。

##### 规则意义
在Go项目中，依赖关系的管理至关重要。未受保护的依赖可能导致第三方库的版本被恶意更改，进而带来安全风险。通过保护模块依赖，我们可以防止意外或恶意修改，确保应用的稳定性和安全性。

##### 错误示例
```go
// 直接在代码中使用了不受保护的模块
import (
    "github.com/example/unsafe-module"
)
```

##### 正确示例
```go
// 使用带有版本锁的Go模块，确保所有依赖的版本是可控的
import (
    "github.com/example/safe-module@v1.2.3"
)
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is designed to ensure that the dependencies of Go modules are not changed without authorization, thereby protecting the integrity of the project's code.

##### Significance of the Rule
In Go projects, managing dependencies is crucial. Unprotected dependencies can lead to the malicious alteration of third-party library versions, resulting in security risks. By protecting module dependencies, we can prevent accidental or malicious modifications, ensuring the stability and security of the application.

##### Error Example
```go
// Directly using an unprotected module in the code
import (
    "github.com/example/unsafe-module"
)
```

##### Correct Example
```go
// Using a version-locked Go module to ensure all dependency versions are controlled
import (
    "github.com/example/safe-module@v1.2.3"
)
```

