rules.content:
#### 规则概述
该规则用于检查并行测试的正确性，确保在执行并行测试时不会出现数据竞争或不稳定的情况。

##### 规则意义
并行测试在提升测试执行速度方面非常有效，但如果未妥善处理共享数据或资源，将导致测试结果不可靠，从而掩盖代码中的缺陷。

##### 错误示例
```go
func TestSomething(t *testing.T) {
    counter++ // 这里可能出现数据竞争
}

func TestParallel(t *testing.T) {
    t.Parallel()
    TestSomething(t)
}
```

##### 正确示例
```go
func TestSomething(t *testing.T, wg *sync.WaitGroup) {
    defer wg.Done()
    localCounter := 0
    localCounter++ // 使用局部变量避免数据竞争
}

func TestParallel(t *testing.T) {
    var wg sync.WaitGroup
    for i := 0; i < 10; i++ {
        wg.Add(1)
        go TestSomething(t, &wg)
    }
    wg.Wait()
}
```

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule is used to check the correctness of parallel testing, ensuring that data races or instability do not occur during the execution of parallel tests.

##### Rule Significance
Parallel testing is very effective in improving the speed of test execution, but if shared data or resources are not handled properly, it can lead to unreliable test results, thus obscuring defects in the code.

##### Incorrect Example
```go
func TestSomething(t *testing.T) {
    counter++ // Data race may occur here
}

func TestParallel(t *testing.T) {
    t.Parallel()
    TestSomething(t)
}
```

##### Correct Example
```go
func TestSomething(t *testing.T, wg *sync.WaitGroup) {
    defer wg.Done()
    localCounter := 0
    localCounter++ // Using a local variable to avoid data races
}

func TestParallel(t *testing.T) {
    var wg sync.WaitGroup
    for i := 0; i < 10; i++ {
        wg.Add(1)
        go TestSomething(t, &wg)
    }
    wg.Wait()
}
```

