#### 规则概述
此规则确保对接收者（receiver）指针的适当使用，尤其是在结构体方法中。

##### 规则意义
在Go语言中，使用值接收者与指针接收者有不同的性能和语义。在一些情况下，使用指针接收者是必要的，以避免对结构体进行值拷贝，尤其是当结构体较大时。合理使用接收者可以提高代码性能和可读性。

##### 错误示例
'''go
package main

type LargeStruct struct {
    A [1000]int
}

func (ls LargeStruct) Method() {
    // 错误：使用值接收者，导致不必要的值拷贝
    println(ls.A[0])
}
'''

##### 正确示例
'''go
package main

type LargeStruct struct {
    A [1000]int
}

func (ls *LargeStruct) Method() {
    // 正确：使用指针接收者，避免值拷贝
    println(ls.A[0])
}
'''

rules.content_en:
#### Rule Overview
This rule ensures the proper use of the receiver pointer, especially in struct methods.

##### Rule Significance
In Go, there are different performance and semantics between value receivers and pointer receivers. In some cases, using a pointer receiver is necessary to avoid value copying of structs, especially when the struct is large. Proper use of receivers can enhance code performance and readability.

##### Incorrect Example
'''go
package main

type LargeStruct struct {
    A [1000]int
}

func (ls LargeStruct) Method() {
    // Incorrect: using a value receiver causes unnecessary value copy
    println(ls.A[0])
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''go
package main

type LargeStruct struct {
    A [1000]int
}

func (ls *LargeStruct) Method() {
    // Correct: using a pointer receiver avoids value copy
    println(ls.A[0])
}
'''

