This rule checks the execution span of functions or methods to ensure they are not overly complex or deeply nested.

##### Rule Meaning
It ensures the readability and maintainability of the code. Complex functions are often difficult to understand and may lead to potential defects and performance issues.

##### Error Example
'''go
func ExampleFunction() {
    for i := 0; i < 1000; i++ {
        for j := 0; j < 1000; j++ {
            // Some complex calculations
            fmt.Println(i * j)
        }
    }
}
'''

##### Correct Example
'''go
func MultiplyAndPrint(limit int) {
    for i := 0; i < limit; i++ {
        PrintMultiplication(i, limit)
    }
}

func PrintMultiplication(i, limit int) {
    for j := 0; j < limit; j++ {
        fmt.Println(i * j)
    }
}
'''

